    "created_at": "2015-10-07T20:20:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-07T20:20:54Z",
    "body": "@Hixie said in whatwg:\n\n> - `<menu type=popup>` is implemented as `<menu type=context>` in Gecko.\n>   This is an unfortunate incompatibility. I renamed \"context\" to \"popup\" \n>   because it doesn't make sense to have `<button type=menu menu=\"\">` \n>   pointing at a `<menu type=context>` since then it's not a context menu \n>   but a drop-down menu. Since both context menus and drop-down menus are \n>   also called \"pop-up menus\" I went with \"popup\". If there's too much \n>   content depending on type=context let me know and I'll change it back.\n\nhttps://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-whatwg-archive/2012Dec/0264.html\n\nThere were ~10,000 pages using type=context in httparchive from last year and 0 type=popup, but the spec was not changed. Since Gecko is shipping this but Blink has it behind a flag, it seems to me we should change back to `context`. The \"make sense\" argument is weak and it's much worse to support two values which is not unlikely if we try to switch to `popup`.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
