    "created_at": "2015-10-07T20:50:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-07T20:50:57Z",
    "body": "The spec was not aligned to follow Gecko's implementation but something else. \n\nI don't think we'll support different behavior for type=popup than for type=context. Either (1) they will be synonyms, in which case I guess the spec should mention them both (but perhaps mention that context is going away, being deprecated?), or (2) we change the spec or (3) we break gecko and keep the spec as it is now (and Gecko adds the synonym). \n\n(1) is ok to me, although the synonym thing is ugly. But I don't know whether other browsers need to then implement type=context too. So (3) is fine too. I'll try to push the Gecko change if needed.\nNaturally (2) is ok too :) \nBut I think I'd prefer (1)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
